From: zolotvok <zolotvok@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 14 Oct 2026 16:30:00 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] panvk: report the kbase node as the DRM primary and render
 node biblioklept

PanVK advertises VK_EXT_physical_device_drm on kbase, but only the DRM
enumeration path fills device->drm, so a /dev/mali* device reported
drmHasPrimary = drmHasRender = VK_FALSE.

gamescope's Wayland backend (the nested compositor DroidDeck runs under
proot) rejects a physical device without both nodes ("physical device
has no primary node" / "has no render node"), then resolves the render
node with drmGetDeviceFromDevId() and opens it. DroidDeck exposes the GPU
character device as /dev/dri/renderD<minor> with a matching
/sys/dev/char/<major>:<minor> tree, the same stand-in the KGSL Turnip it
ships reports. Report the kbase node's st_rdev as both nodes so that
stand-in can be found. Mesa's Wayland WSI also compares this dev_t with
the compositor's dma-buf feedback main device, so the stand-in avoids the
PRIME blit copy.

panvk_can_present_on_device() does not read these fields.

Purpose: VK_EXT_physical_device_drm on kbase for gamescope and dma-buf feedback (DroidDeck Linux runtime); biblioklept
Source/Reference: gamescope 3.16 src/rendervulkan.cpp CVulkanDevice::createDevice (hasPrimary/hasRender checks, drmGetDeviceFromDevId); DroidDeck LinuxRuntime.bindGpuNode
Tested GPU: Mali-G1-Ultra MC12 (v14, gpu_id 0xe8800010), vivo X300 Pro
Tested Kbase UAPI: CSF 1.38
Mesa base range: 5a07217f
Dependencies: kbase-common/004 (panvk_physical_device_init_kbase), applies before jm-v9
Validation test: VkPhysicalDeviceDrmPropertiesEXT on /dev/mali0 reports hasPrimary = hasRender = 1 with the node's major:minor (10:293 on the vivo X300 Pro)

Generated-by: LLM
---
 src/panfrost/vulkan/panvk_physical_device.c | 6 ++++++
 1 file changed, 6 insertions(+)

diff --git a/src/panfrost/vulkan/panvk_physical_device.c b/src/panfrost/vulkan/panvk_physical_device.c
index 3e82eff..0e4c79b 100644
--- a/src/panfrost/vulkan/panvk_physical_device.c
+++ b/src/panfrost/vulkan/panvk_physical_device.c
@@ -1378,6 +1378,12 @@ panvk_physical_device_init_kbase(struct panvk_physical_device *device,
    if (result != VK_SUCCESS)
       return result;
 
+   struct stat st;
+   if (stat(path, &st) == 0 && S_ISCHR(st.st_mode)) {
+      device->drm.primary_rdev = st.st_rdev;
+      device->drm.render_rdev = st.st_rdev;
+   }
+
    device->model = pan_get_model(device->kmod.dev->props.gpu_id,
                                  device->kmod.dev->props.gpu_variant);
 
